# ProductEditor – Revert to Minimal Working Version

When **changes didn't work** and the **page is still blank**, revert `ProductEditor.tsx` to a known minimal working state.

## IMMEDIATE ACTION

1. Open **ProductEditor.tsx**.
2. **Replace the ENTIRE file** with this minimal working version:

```typescript
'use client'

import { useParams } from 'next/navigation'
import { useEffect, useState } from 'react'
import { createClient } from '@/lib/supabase/client'
import { useAuth } from '@clerk/nextjs'

export default function ProductEditor() {
  const params = useParams()
  const { userId } = useAuth()
  const productId = params.id as string

  const [product, setProduct] = useState<any>(null)
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true)

  useEffect(() => {
    async function loadProduct() {
      if (!productId || !userId) return

      const supabase = createClient()
      const { data } = await supabase
        .from('products')
        .select('*')
        .eq('id', productId)
        .eq('user_id', userId)
        .single()

      setProduct(data)
      setLoading(false)
    }

    loadProduct()
  }, [productId, userId])

  if (loading) {
    return (
      <div className="flex items-center justify-center h-screen bg-gray-900 text-white">
        <div>Loading product...</div>
      </div>
    )
  }

  if (!product) {
    return (
      <div className="flex items-center justify-center h-screen bg-gray-900 text-white">
        <div>Product not found</div>
      </div>
    )
  }

  return (
    <div className="h-screen bg-gray-900 text-white flex flex-col">
      {/* Header */}
      <header className="border-b border-gray-800 p-4 flex justify-between items-center">
        <h1 className="text-xl font-bold">{product.title}</h1>
        <button className="px-4 py-2 bg-orange-500 rounded">
          Export
        </button>
      </header>

      {/* Main Content */}
      <div className="flex-1 overflow-auto p-8">
        <div className="max-w-4xl mx-auto bg-white text-black p-8 rounded shadow-lg">
          <div dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: product.content }} />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  )
}
```

3. **Save the file.**
4. **DO NOT** add any other code.
5. This is the **absolute minimum** to show the product.

## If this doesn't work

Then the problem is in **data loading** (API, auth, or Supabase), not the UI. Debug the data layer next (e.g. API route, Supabase table, or Clerk `userId`).

## If this works

The previous complex editor was the source of the blank page. Reintroduce features **gradually** (e.g. one panel or one feature at a time) and test after each change.
